WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.083
-What exactly are you asking of me?
-I suppose I'm asking you to look into it.

00:00:04.166 --> 00:00:06.541
Look into what, exactly?

00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:09.166
Look into St. Patrick's?

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:11.916
On… And just to be clear,

00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:15.416
on the basis that some
of your mother's blood tests got damaged?

00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:17.791
-It's a lot to ask, I know.
-Do you?

00:00:18.791 --> 00:00:19.666
[Sarah sighs]

00:00:20.708 --> 00:00:21.541
Do you?

00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:27.291
[clicks tongue] Did I ever tell you
why I moved here?

00:00:28.291 --> 00:00:30.291
No. No, I don't think you did.

00:00:31.041 --> 00:00:33.416
Didn't tell anybody,
now that I think about it.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:37.416
It's almost as if nobody asked.

00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:43.208
You know, I was, um, 21
when the Towers went down.

00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:46.666
Watched it on TV
in my dorm room just weepin'.

00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:51.916
When I was a kid,
I wasn't religious at all, really.

00:00:53.166 --> 00:00:56.833
But I went to the mosque that day,
because they had a blood drive,

00:00:57.458 --> 00:00:59.208
and the line went for blocks.

00:00:59.916 --> 00:01:00.916
I wanted to help.

00:01:02.416 --> 00:01:05.166
I wanted to protect this country.

00:01:06.291 --> 00:01:10.541
So I moved to New York
and enrolled in NYPD training.

00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:12.791
Now, some of my friends,
they weren't happy.

00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:18.208
"NYPD is against us," they'd say.
But I'd tell them, "No. You're wrong."

00:01:19.208 --> 00:01:21.916
"I'll show them
they don't have to be afraid of us."

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:24.583
"I'll show them who we are."

00:01:26.041 --> 00:01:27.291
So I worked my way up.

00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:32.958
You know, traffic, and translating
and transcribing wiretaps, then Vice.

00:01:33.041 --> 00:01:38.041
I get married. Ali is born,
and I'm promoted again. Detective now.

00:01:39.416 --> 00:01:44.291
Top secret security clearance
for the joint terrorism task force.

00:01:44.416 --> 00:01:48.041
I'm helping the FBI fight terrorists.

00:01:49.666 --> 00:01:54.166
We're taking collars. You know,
petty stuff, pot, parking tickets

00:01:54.208 --> 00:01:56.416
and leaning on them hard
if they're Muslim.

00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:59.708
"You know, we'll drop the charge,
help you out."

00:01:59.791 --> 00:02:01.416
"You go to the mosque and listen."

00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:04.833
I thought we were
supposed to be fighting terrorists.

00:02:05.916 --> 00:02:09.916
Not flipping some pothead student
in Queens to spy on Americans.

00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:12.833
So I complain.

00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:16.166
Gently. One time.

00:02:17.958 --> 00:02:18.916
Everything changed.

00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:22.583
I was surveilled by other cops.

00:02:23.166 --> 00:02:25.416
I mean, they even had
an official file on me.

00:02:27.166 --> 00:02:30.208
And not just me.
See, like, after the Towers,

00:02:30.791 --> 00:02:34.416
Muslim officers were promoted fast.
Especially if we knew the language,

00:02:34.458 --> 00:02:37.041
like, linguistic knowledge,
cultural knowledge.

00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:39.708
We were very desirable for that.

00:02:40.708 --> 00:02:42.416
But it started to occur to them,

00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:48.416
with so many of us on the force,
elevated to positions of real authority,

00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:52.291
what if that had been our plan all along?

00:02:55.083 --> 00:02:56.541
What if we were interlopers?

00:02:57.833 --> 00:02:59.416
What if we were infiltrators?

00:03:00.291 --> 00:03:05.791
What if we were double agents?
And they fucking panicked.

00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:09.291
Internal Affairs was suddenly all over us.
We were being followed.

00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:13.041
We're being recorded. Civilians too.
Surveilled at mosques, cafes.

00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:17.083
And suddenly I'm out of plain clothes
and I'm back in uniform.

00:03:18.916 --> 00:03:20.583
Night shift, street beat.

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:25.083
And more and more,
I realize I've lost their trust.

00:03:30.291 --> 00:03:31.083
I roll with it.

00:03:32.291 --> 00:03:33.416
I keep my head high.

00:03:35.208 --> 00:03:36.041
Dignity.

00:03:41.666 --> 00:03:43.666
Dignity is a word my wife uses.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.416
"Show them dignity."

00:03:49.416 --> 00:03:51.041
And then she's diagnosed.

00:03:53.416 --> 00:03:57.458
And she's robbed of her dignity so fast.

00:04:00.583 --> 00:04:01.791
And then she's gone.

00:04:02.583 --> 00:04:03.541
And I couldn't…

00:04:07.958 --> 00:04:12.083
Ali and I get as far away as we can.
And I find this gig.

00:04:12.916 --> 00:04:14.041
This little island.

00:04:15.333 --> 00:04:18.916
So sleepy, it could be dead.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:25.291
No elections, no staff. Just a tiny room
at the back of a grocery store,

00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:29.416
and a bunch of fishermen without a notable
incident of intentional violence

00:04:29.541 --> 00:04:33.333
in almost a century,
and I beg for the post.

00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:36.416
Dignity.

00:04:39.791 --> 00:04:41.958
Ali is bored to tears.

00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:43.791
But he's safe.

00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:51.083
And I still think I could
maybe move the world that one millimeter.

00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:55.333
You know, maybe here's
where we make a difference.

00:04:55.416 --> 00:04:58.291
Not in the big city,
but in this tiny village.

00:04:59.041 --> 00:05:02.416
Win over the fucking PTA
and call it a victory for Islam.

00:05:03.541 --> 00:05:04.666
So I don't intimidate.

00:05:07.041 --> 00:05:12.291
I don't overshare
or overstep or intrude in any way.

00:05:13.208 --> 00:05:14.708
I don't even carry a gun.

00:05:16.958 --> 00:05:17.916
And still…

00:05:19.791 --> 00:05:20.666
Still…

00:05:21.833 --> 00:05:25.291
Beverly Keane and a few others too

00:05:26.208 --> 00:05:29.541
look at me like
I'm Osama bin-Fucking-Laden.

00:05:31.958 --> 00:05:33.208
And you'd like me

00:05:34.416 --> 00:05:36.125
to investigate St. Patrick's?

